{"id": "unknown-2026-10-21-009", "date": "2026-10-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India, US ‘pretty close’ to trade deal: Trump", "content": "US President Trump said India and the US were close to finalising a bilateral trade agreement, describing it as different from previous deals. \nHis remarks came as US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is visiting India to discuss trade, energy, technology and defence. \nRubio said only a few issues remained unresolved and expressed confidence that the pact would be finalised shortly.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-us-pretty-close-to-trade-deal-trump-314390-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-21-010", "date": "2026-10-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton extends gains as weak dollar, firm crude lend support", "content": "ICE cotton December 2026 futures settled at 80.88 cents per pound, up 0.94 per cent, as a weaker US dollar and stronger crude oil supported export competitiveness and cotton's edge over synthetics.\nGains were capped by expectations of an accelerated US harvest, with USDA reporting 41 per cent picked, ahead of the five-year average.\nVolume rose 14 per cent, but trade stayed subdued.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-extends-gains-as-weak-dollar-firm-crude-lend-support-314389-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-21-011", "date": "2026-10-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India-New Zealand FTA takes effect, opens duty-free textile access", "content": "India-New Zealand FTA took effect on October 20, opening duty-free access in New Zealand for Indian textiles, apparel, leather and footwear. \nNew Zealand removed duties on all Indian export tariff lines, including peak tariffs of up to 10 per cent; faster customs are expected to lower landed costs. \nThe pact backs a 2030 goal to double goods and services trade to NZ$7 billion ($3.99 billion). ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-new-zealand-fta-takes-effect-opens-duty-free-textile-access-314385-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
